/* Search en français.

   Each key is the English the code says; macOS shows this file's words
   when French comes first in System Settings › General › Language & Region,
   for the whole Mac or for Search alone, and the English otherwise. A key
   missing here falls back to its English, so nothing is ever blank.

   Grouped by the file the words first appear in. The vocabulary follows
   macOS and Safari in French: Réglages, signets, trousseau, clés
   d'identification. Typography: a no-break space before ? ! : ; and inside
   « », curly apostrophes. A %@ or %lld keeps its place, or names it
   (%1$@, %2$@) when French turns the sentence around. */


